  "body_html": "<h1>Nash Payoff Uniqueness in Zero-Sum Games</h1>\n<p>In a zero-sum game, any two Nash equilibria give the same payoff to player 0\nand the same payoff to player 1.  Thus the equilibrium payoff is a value of the\ngame, independent of which Nash equilibrium is chosen.</p>\n<p>The proof compares two equilibria through cross profiles.  One player's best\nresponse inequality is converted into the other player's inequality using\nzero-sum payoff negation.</p>",
